  "redResult": {
    "newTests": {
      "tests": 14,
      "pass": 6,
      "fail": 8
    },
    "failingTests": [
      "the pet window opts into living above the macOS menu bar",
      "the pet window is raised to the status level above the menu bar at startup",
      "an alert keeps the status level instead of dropping the pet behind the menu bar",
      "a saved position above the menu bar is restored verbatim",
      "saved-position validation uses full bounds and falls back to workArea only when a display lacks bounds",
      "a drag off every display is pulled back by the minimal margin and the corrected position is reported",
      "47 pt of the pet visible after a drag is clamped by the minimal margin",
      "the drag guard also applies in unmanaged mode"
    ],
    "summary": "The 8 failing assertions exist because the pre-change src/main.cjs lacks all four new behaviors: enableLargerThanScreen is undefined, no setAlwaysOnTop(true, 'status') at startup or in raiseAlertWindow (a bare setAlwaysOnTop(true) downgrades to 'floating'), saved-position validation only measures workArea (so saved y=-200 is rejected), and the debounced drag-end handler only reports position without a full-bounds minimal-clamp reachability guard. The 6 passing new tests are regression guards that must stay green (48 pt boundary, full-bounds-reachable above-bar position, multi-display reachability, guarded no-ops for minimal/missing APIs, and R5 default placement + IPC surface).",
    "preExistingSuite": {
      "command": "npm test before the new file was added",
      "tests": 149,
      "pass": 149,
      "fail": 0
    }
  },
  "revision": 1,
  "revisionNote": "Increment 3 test-author handoff. New protected acceptance test test/window-above-menubar.test.cjs (14 tests: 8 genuine RED against the pre-change src/main.cjs, 6 passing regression guards). No production behavior changed in this phase; the src/main.cjs sha256 is the PRE-change scaffold hash, frozen only as RED evidence, and is expected to change during implementation. Requirement set: user-approved Option A, pet may live above the macOS menu bar (R1 enableLargerThanScreen, R2 setAlwaysOnTop(true, 'status') at creation and in raiseAlertWindow, R3 saved-position validation against FULL display bounds with workArea fallback when a display has no bounds, R4 debounced drag-end reachability guard with VISIBLE_MARGIN = 48 pt minimal clamp against the most-intersecting display / primary when none intersect, R5 unchanged default and off-screen placement and IPC surface)."
}
